WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.910
1979.

2
00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.490
A professor of mathematical physics
at Cambridge resigns his chair.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.000
He trains for the Anglican
priesthood, and is ordained in 1982.

4
00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.620
His name is John Polkinghorne.

5
00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:17.900
Biologist Richard Dawkins treats
God as a scientific hypothesis,

6
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.910
testable like any other.

7
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:24.570
Oxford theologian Alister McGrath,
once an atheist, disagrees.

8
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.450
Can a top physicist also be a priest?

9
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.620
And what can science
prove, and what can't it?

10
00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:34.320
In this mission, you'll map four ways
of relating science and religion,

11
00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:36.790
and see where each thinker stands.

12
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.720
Then you'll weigh up a sharp claim:
that a scientist must be an atheist.

13
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:45.610
Your mission: find out what
science can and can't prove,

14
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.230
and what that means for faith.
